  "name": "Larakaraka and bwola (Acholi courtship and royal dances)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Two of the principal dances of the Acholi of northern Uganda. Larakaraka is the courtship and wedding dance, in which young men and women dance in lines to singing and percussion, and bwola is the royal dance of the chiefdoms, in which men beat small drums as they dance in a wide circle around a leader while women dance within it. The membrane-drum card stands in for the Acholi drums.",
